//github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/pull/12279/changes delete some comments, please add it back, now I don't know about the `fresh-mode` in the PR title.
What is the differences between FIXED_BASE_REF and FIXED_BASE_SHA, the naming don't show the real meaning.
Good point. `FIXED_BASE_REF` was the ref used to fetch the upstream commit, while `FIXED_BASE_SHA` was the immutable commit actually used as the rebase base. I renamed them to `UPSTREAM_FETCH_REF` and `UPSTREAM_REBASE_SHA` and added a comment to make the distinction explicit. In fresh mode, both are empty because the workflow checks out the resolved upstream SHA directly.
